From: WhaleOS <whaleos-dev@navercorp.com>
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Fix /data noexec: rbind,exec and inject init.waydroid.rc

ChromeOS encrypts the stateful partition (encstateful) and always mounts
it with noexec.  Our waydroid work directory lives under
/usr/local/var/lib/waydroid (set by patch 0008), and on ChromeOS
/usr/local/var is a system-level symlink to /var, so the work dir
resolves to /var/lib/waydroid -- i.e. on encstateful and inherits
noexec.  Android's vold/init then re-mounts /data from the encstateful
block device, also inheriting noexec, which prevents dlopen() of native
libraries installed under /data/app.

Two fixes in tools/helpers/lxc.py:

1. Add exec to the rbind options for the waydroid_data bind-mount so the
   initial LXC mount is already exec-capable.

2. Bind-mount /usr/lib/waydroid/data/configs/init.waydroid.rc over
   system/etc/init/init.waydroid.rc before Android init runs.  The
   injected RC file adds an "exec -- /system/bin/mount -o remount,exec
   /data" in the post-fs-data stage so that even after vold re-mounts
   /data with noexec the flag is stripped before any app code runs.

--- a/tools/helpers/lxc.py
+++ b/tools/helpers/lxc.py
@@ -210,2 +210,3 @@
-    if not make_entry(session["waydroid_data"], "data", options="rbind 0 0"):
+    if not make_entry(session["waydroid_data"], "data", options="rbind,exec 0 0"):
         raise OSError("Failed to bind userdata")
+    make_entry("/usr/lib/waydroid/data/configs/init.waydroid.rc", "system/etc/init/init.waydroid.rc")
